## Pipeline Eval Harness (1 archived, 6 retained)

Implement v1 of the eval harness per `docs/PLAN_eval-harness.md` (v8). Split into seven sequential tasks sized for context boundaries; each task compiles and tests pass independently. Run order: E1.1 -> E1.2 -> E1.3 -> E1.4 -> E1.5 -> E1.6 -> E1.7.

- [x] E1.1: Foundation -- run manifest types, JSONL parser, run loader, stage canonicalization. Implementation per `docs/PLAN_eval-harness.md` (v8) steps 0, 2, 3, 4. This is the data plane: types and parsers, no orchestrator wiring yet. After this task the codebase compiles with new modules but no behavior change. [QRP!B-]

  Files (CREATE):
  - `src/run_manifest.rs` -- public types: `RunManifest`, `ManifestHandle` (`Arc<std::sync::Mutex<RunManifest>>`), `PromptEvidenceSpec`, `StageInvocationId(u64)`, `StageStatus { Ran, Skipped, Reused, CheckpointResume, Failed }`, `ArtifactSource { ThisRun, Checkpoint, PreviousRun }`, `CompletionPath { AuditPass, AuditFail, AuditSkipped, BuilderFailure, PlannerFailure, Aborted }`, `AgentExitInfo { log_path: Option<PathBuf>, actual_provider: String, actual_model: String, fallback_reason: Option<String> }`. Public methods on `ManifestHandle`: `record_invocation(spec) -> StageInvocationId`, `record_exit(id, status, exit_observed_at, exit_info)`, `record_skip(stage_id, role, status, skip_reason, artifact_source) -> StageInvocationId`, `mark_superseded(prior_id, by_id)`, `record_completion(completion_path)`, `flush() -> Result<()>`. All take `&self`. Atomic flush via `.tmp` + rename. Use `blake3 = "1"` (already in Cargo.toml:26) for `system_prompt_hash` / `user_prompt_hash`; label as `blake3:<hex>`. Compute at `record_invocation` time: `system_prompt_bytes` and `user_prompt_bytes` (raw byte length); `prompt_pattern_ids_found` (substring match `[<pattern_id>]` per `src/patterns.rs:366`); `prompt_artifact_refs_found` (basename match against `prior_artifact_paths`); `prompt_extension_names_found` (substring match `--- BEGIN EXTENSION CONTEXT: {name} ---` per `src/extensions.rs:192`). Manifest serializes to `.buildloop/run-manifest.json`.
  - `src/eval/mod.rs` -- module entry. Public `pub fn run_for_current_task(project_dir: &Path) -> anyhow::Result<()>`. **For E1.1 this is a stub returning `Ok(())`**; real implementation lands in E1.5.
  - `src/eval/parser.rs` -- `StageTranscript { stage_id, log_path, model_from_init, tools_from_init, tool_uses, tool_results, assistant_messages, exit_observed, parser_skipped: bool }`. `parse_stage_log(path) -> Result<StageTranscript>`. Walks Claude SDK JSONL: extracts `system/init` events (model, tools), iterates `assistant.message.content[]` for `tool_use` items (record `name`, `input`, `parent_tool_use_id`), `tool_result` items, and assistant text. Resilient to malformed lines (skip + log via `tracing::warn` or eprintln). Non-Claude logs (e.g. `studio-codex-*.jsonl`) return `parser_skipped: true` with empty `tool_uses` so checks Skip cleanly.
  - `src/eval/run.rs` -- `RunTranscripts { manifest: RunManifest, invocations: Vec<(StageInvocation, StageTranscript)> }`. `latest_run(buildloop_dir: &Path) -> Result<RunTranscripts>` reads `.buildloop/run-manifest.json` and loads each invocation's JSONL by `log_path`. Invocations with `status` in `{Skipped, Reused, CheckpointResume}` get a stub `StageTranscript` with `parser_skipped: true` and empty fields. Failed invocations with `log_path: None` get the same.
  - `src/eval/stage_id.rs` -- `enum StageId { Query, Research, Plan, Build, Audit }` with `#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]` and `#[serde(rename_all = "lowercase")]` plus `#[serde(rename = "implement")]` on `Build` and `#[serde(rename = "doubt")]` on `Audit`. `from_log_prefix(&str) -> Option<StageId>` handles `SCOUT, QUERY, RESEARCH, PLAN, IMPLEMENT, VERIFY, P+, DISCOVERY` and legacy `PLANNER, BUILDER, REVIEWER, FIXER`. `from_role(AgentRole) -> Option<StageId>`. Hard-coded `pub fn prior_artifact(stage: StageId) -> Option<&'static str>` map: Q -> None; R -> ".buildloop/questions.md"; P -> ".buildloop/research-report.md"; B -> ".buildloop/current-plan.md"; A -> ".buildloop/build-claims.md".

