  Files (CREATE):
  - `src/eval/checks/mod.rs` -- `Check` trait per PLAN.md step 5: `fn name(&self) -> &str`, `fn category(&self) -> Category`, `fn severity(&self) -> Severity`, `fn applies_to(&self) -> &[StageId]`, `fn run(&self, run: &RunTranscripts) -> Vec<StageCheckResult>`. Types: `Category { Plumbing, Heuristic }`, `Severity { Critical, Standard }`, `StageCheckResult { stage: StageId, status: Status, evidence: String }`, `Status { Pass, Fail, Skip }`. Skip rule per PLAN.md: checks Skip with evidence when invocation status is `Skipped|Reused|CheckpointResume`; checks grade normally on `Ran` or `Failed`. Static check registry as `pub fn all_checks() -> Vec<Box<dyn Check>>` returning the 16 checks.
  - `src/eval/checks/plumbing.rs` -- 8 checks per PLAN.md step 6:
    - `stage_completed_successfully` (Critical) -- invocation `status` is `Ran`. Fails on `Failed`.
    - `system_prompt_present` (Critical) -- `system_prompt_bytes > 0`. NOT just hash non-empty (`blake3("")` is `af1349b9...`, a non-empty hash).
    - `model_matches_config` -- pass if `effective_provider/model == originally_configured_provider/model` AND `override_reason` is null. Skip when `override_reason` is set (e.g. `"budget_recovery"`); evidence names the reason.
    - `extension_loaded` -- `prompt_extension_names_found` contains every entry from `selected_extension_names`. Skip if `selected_extension_names` is empty.
    - `patterns_injected` -- `prompt_pattern_ids_found` contains every `matched_pattern_ids`. Skip if no patterns matched.
    - `prior_artifact_received` (Critical) -- for stages B>1, `prompt_artifact_refs_found` contains stage N-1's artifact basename (per `stage_id::prior_artifact` map).
    - `prior_artifact_read` (Standard, **Claude-only**) -- the parser walks `assistant.message.content[]` for `tool_use` records with `name == "Read"`. Passes if any record has `input.file_path` ending in the prior artifact's basename. Subagent-issued reads (records carrying `parent_tool_use_id`) count. Skip with evidence "non-Claude provider, transcript adapter not in v1" when `actual_provider != "claude"` OR `parser_skipped == true`. Keys on `actual_provider`, not `effective_provider`, so Codex->Claude fallback parses correctly.
    - `expected_artifact_written` -- manifest's `expected_artifact_path` exists on disk with > 200 bytes.
  - `src/eval/checks/heuristic.rs` -- 8 checks per PLAN.md step 7:
    - `plan_covers_research_files` -- every file path in `research-report.md` appears in `current-plan.md`.
    - `plan_has_verification` -- `current-plan.md` has a verification section with at least one command.
    - `build_claims_has_files_changed` -- `## Files Changed` with at least one `[CREATE|MODIFY]` line per `src/prompts.rs:592-610`.
    - `build_claims_has_verification_results` -- `## Verification Results` with PASS/FAIL/SKIPPED for Build, Tests, Lint.
    - `build_claims_files_exist` -- every path under `## Files Changed` exists on disk.
    - `build_claims_has_gaps_section` -- `## Gaps and Assumptions` is present.
    - `audit_engaged` -- parse `review-report.md` markdown, locate the fenced ```json code block, parse the inner object per `src/prompts.rs:941`, confirm at least one of `high`/`medium`/`low` is non-empty OR the verdict is explicit PASS with rationale. Skip if `audit_skipped_reason` is set.
    - `audit_findings_localized` -- when findings exist, each entry in `high`/`medium`/`low` has `file` and `line` fields per the reviewer schema.
  - `src/eval/scorer.rs` -- aggregate per stage. `enum StageBadge { Pass, Warn, Fail, Skipped }` rendered as `✓ ⚠ ✗ -`. Status thresholds: `✓` all checks pass; `⚠` any heuristic fail or any non-critical plumbing fail; `✗` any Critical plumbing fail; `-` stage status is `Skipped|Reused|CheckpointResume`. Aggregate badge string in QRPBA order, e.g. `EVAL Q✓R✓P✓B⚠A✓`. Aggregation rule: per stage, take the worst status across all checks for **non-superseded invocations only**; superseded invocations appear in the overlay but don't contribute to the badge. Multipass review never sets `superseded_by`, so all per-file passes count.
  - `src/eval/report.rs` -- `write_report(transcripts: &RunTranscripts, scores: &Scores, project_dir: &Path) -> Result<()>` writes `.buildloop/eval-report.json` with `schema_version: 1`, `run_id`, `task_id`, `generated_at`, per-stage scores (including stage status + skip_reason + artifact_source), every check's status + evidence per invocation, aggregate badge, manifest's `completion_path`, and a `notes: Vec<String>` array (e.g. `["1 stage ran under budget_recovery override", "1 stage uses codex-doubt; manifest evidence is degraded"]`). Idempotent: re-running on the same manifest + logs produces a byte-identical report (modulo `generated_at`).

